{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-volume-tower-decomposition","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:volume-tower-decomposition","kind":"proposition","title":"Tower-level decomposition of hyperbolic volume","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-cosimplicial-crossed-groupoid"],"tags":["hyperbolic-volume","cosimplicial","brane-tower","quantum-dilogarithm","spectral-sequence"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.Archimedean.VolumeTowerDecomposition","text":"volume-tower-decomposition.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:volume-tower-decomposition\"></a><p><em>The hyperbolic volume of any knot <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">K</code> decomposes exactly into tower-level Chern-Simons integrals:</em></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\mathrm{Vol}(K)\n  = \\sum_{n=0}^{\\infty} \\Phi_n(K).</code></pre>\n<p><em>Each <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Phi_n(K)</code> evaluates the Chern-Simons 3-form over the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n</code>-th twisted sector. The sum converges absolutely.</em></p>\n<p>The Yekutieli triple determines the integration data at each level. The coface map connects consecutive terms. In the classical limit <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q \\to 1</code>, the tower collapses. All higher terms vanish, leaving only the exact hyperbolic volume <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Phi_0(K) = \\mathrm{Vol}(K)</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/volume-tower-decomposition.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"13.38.4","page":"b/prop-volume-tower-decomposition","qa":{"counts":{"pass":88,"fail":2,"warn":1,"na":13,"unknown":0,"stale":78},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.MassTheory.Archimedean.VolumeTowerDecomposition","via":"ref","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
